>>>  Oh, and while we are at it, remember you can make a few artifacts 
>>> yourself. How much do you want to be spoiled?

There more artifacts are generated in the game, the harder it becomes to 
   get new ones. Therefore the only artifact that should be made by 
yourself is Excalibur, since it's not the best of them but it's ease of 
acquirement in early game makes it highly useful.

The other two (Orcrist and Sting) are utterly worthless, in previous 
versions where artifacts sold for more you could've used them as a means 
  to get money if you needed it desperately but nowadays they just add 
to your artifact counter and make it harder to get the ones you're 
looking for.

Unless your character is able to advance in skill with your choice 
artifact, I suggest not wishing for them because having your god grant 
you a weapon (via sacrificing) also gives you proficiency in it, which 
wishing for it does not. Since samurai have high skills in all weapons 
it doesn't really matter, tho =)

Yeah, instead of playing for years to find out stuff in Nethack you can 
look just about anything up in here: 
http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/nethack/spoilerlist.html


